DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddiiggiittttooiinntt() and ddiiggiittttooiinntt__ll() functions convert a numeric character
     to its corresponding integer value.  The character can be any decimal
     digit or hexadecimal digit.  With hexadecimal characters, the case of the
     values does not matter.

     The ddiiggiittttooiinntt__ll() function takes an explicit locale argument, whereas
     the ddiiggiittttooiinntt() function use the current global or per-thread locale.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ddiiggiittttooiinntt() and ddiiggiittttooiinntt__ll() functions always return an integer
     from the range of 0 to 15.  If the given character was not a digit as de‐
     fined by isxdigit(3) or isxdigit_l(3), the function will return 0.

